/target

# Local semantic-search index for the omniscient MCP tool. It is untracked
# scratch state, not source — and cargo's packaging step sweeps in *any*
# untracked file that isn't gitignored, git repo or not. Without this line,
# `cargo package`/`cargo publish` picked up ~900 of this directory's index
# files (transaction logs, manifests) alongside the ~20 files that actually
# belong in the crate. Found via `cargo package --list` while wiring up the
# release pipeline; see release.toml and release-plz.toml.
/.omniscient/

# Working documents live on disk, not in git.
#
# Plans are consumed during execution and superseded by the commits they
# produce; tracking them creates merge conflicts over files nobody reads
# again. Specs and the superpowers workspace are the same shape of artifact —
# they are how the work gets thought through, not the work's output.
#
# NOTE: git history still holds every version committed before this rule, so
# nothing written so far is lost — `git log --diff-filter=D -- <path>` finds
# it. But from here on these paths exist only on disk, so treat
# `git clean -fdx` with care.
/docs/plans/
/docs/specs/
/docs/superpowers/
